Towards the player and NPC issue, it seems I havent made myself
understood. 

By keeping player's body as NPC after a player has logged out, I mean
the player should connect to the same body when he log in next time.
He may find himself not in the same place as last time he quitted. But
that doesnt matter very much. As long as one player has a persistent
name and body, it will work.

If every NPC can act like player, there will be too much load for the
CPU because even if nobody plays, the mud is working by itself. Imagin
a mud with thousand NPCs moving around... too much load for the CPU.
It also adds the difficulty to the programmers. 
Currently, all the mud objects are 'recycled' if they are not used 
recently. This is done by the 'clean_up' function. And this functionality
will keep those necessary rooms and NPCs in memory and CPU doesnt need to
work on unnecessary stuffs in order to speed up the overall performance.


